# Midterm - Implement ls(1)

This project implements the subset of NetBSD ls(1) specified by the
midterm manual page.

## Build
    make

## Usage
    ./ls [ -AacdFfhiklnqRrSstuw ] [file ...]

## Main tests
    ./ls
    ./ls -a
    ./ls -A
    ./ls -l
    ./ls -n
    ./ls -i
    ./ls -F
    ./ls -R
    ./ls -r
    ./ls -S
    ./ls -t
    ./ls -s
    ./ls -h -l
    ./ls -d .
    ./ls -f
    ./ls -w

## Testing notes
The output was compared manually with the behavior described in the
provided ls(1) manual. Tests include regular files, hidden files,
directories, executable files, symbolic links, sorting, recursive
listing, long format, inode numbers, block counts and human-readable
sizes.
